WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.200
-We have exactly six shows left
before we go on Christmas break,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.567
which means it's time
for that beloved

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:05.834
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:09.167
It is time for "12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters."

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:10.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:12.167
-♪ Twelve Days of
Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:16.033
♪ Six days left ♪

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:19.100
-That's right, every show
between now and Christmas,

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.267
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:23.534
a whopper of a Christmas sweater

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:26.734
from the Countdown to Christmas
Cabinet.

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:28.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.300
Since there are six shows left,
let's open door number six.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.100
-Ready?
-I'm ready for this.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.133
-I'm always ready.
-I'm ready.

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.701
-I appreciate this.
-Good. Ready?

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:39.400
[ Drum roll ]

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.834
♪♪

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:49.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.501
-I like this one. I like this.

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.868
Flowy.

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:57.634
Flowy, subtle.

00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:59.100
I like this a lot.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:02.400
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.234
Everyone,
look at your seat number.

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:05.968
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:07.701
Quest, can I get a drum roll,
please?

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:12.834
[ Drum roll ]

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:15.501
2-8-2!

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:17.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.534
Yes! Come on, bud.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:24.968
♪♪

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:30.400
♪♪

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.167
Yes, yes, yes!

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:34.667
Nice to see you, bud.

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:35.968
How are you?

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:37.701
Nice to see you, pal.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.133
Congratulations.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.167
What is your name
and where are you from?

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:44.934
-Ken Kavanaugh
from Austin, Texas.

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:46.334
-Yes!

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:47.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:50.534
Austin, Texas. We love it.

00:01:50.534 --> 00:01:52.100
It does get a little chilly out
there in Texas

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.100
every now and then.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.300
-Yes, it does.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.300
Do you have anything like this
that you could --

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.501
[ Light laughter ]
-No, I do not.

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:57.701
-No, you don't.
Would you like to try it on

00:01:57.701 --> 00:01:59.100
right now for everyone?

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.534
Speaking about keeping it weird,
we've got to keep it weird,

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:02.634
Austin.

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:04.000
♪♪

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.868
Hang on. Here you go.

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:07.901
-Yeah!

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:08.934
[ Cheering ]

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.234
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:11.234
That's perfect.

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:14.334
Oh! Oh, this is perfect.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.434
Are you kidding me?

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:16.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:19.234
This is --
that's what you wear out.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:21.367
This is fantastic.

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:22.968
One more time,
give him a round of applause.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.234
Stick around.
We'll be right back.

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:26.133
Congratulations. Happy Holidays.

